# No Em Dashes

Never use the em dash character (`—`) in any output: chat replies, emails, LinkedIn messages, resumes, docs, comments, or commit messages.

It is a common AI tell. Do not use it.

## Use instead

- Commas
- Periods / separate sentences
- Colons
- Parentheses
- A normal hyphen (`-`) only for compound words or date ranges (e.g. `Dec 2025 - Present`)

## Examples

Bad: `I'm interested — thanks for reaching out.`

Good: `I'm interested. Thanks for reaching out.`

Bad: `Deploy releases — then validate on the floor.`

Good: `Deploy releases, then validate on the floor.`

## Check before sending

Before finishing any user-facing text, scan for `—` and rewrite those spots.
